\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 SCRIPT DESCRIPTIONS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Script 1 \'97 GeoNet earthquake catalogue\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Downloads or combines monthly GeoNet earthquake catalogue files, standardises column types, removes duplicated earthquake identifiers, and creates the master earthquake catalogue.\
Main output:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_raw/geonet_catalogue.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 2 \'97 Felt RAPID observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Queries the GeoNet Felt RAPID API for eligible earthquakes, caches the query results, retains spatial intensity cells and MMI count distributions, and joins earthquake-level Felt RAPID summaries to the catalogue.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_raw/felt_rapid_observations.parquet\
data_raw/felt_rapid_mmi_counts.parquet\
data_raw/felt_rapid_query_status.parquet\
data_processed/catalogue_with_felt_summary.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 3 \'97 Moment-tensor information\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Downloads the GeoNet centroid moment-tensor catalogue, cleans its fields, identifies preferred solutions where multiple solutions exist, derives broad fault-style classifications, and joins the preferred solution to the Felt-enriched catalogue.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_raw/moment_tensor_all_solutions.parquet\
data_raw/moment_tensor.parquet\
data_processed/catalogue_with_felt_mt.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 4 \'97 Strong-motion observations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Queries the GeoNet processed strong-motion API for eligible earthquakes. It retains station-level PGA, PGV, MMI, station coordinates, and distance information. Query results are cached so later runs only request newly eligible or previously failed earthquakes.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_raw/strong_motion_observations.parquet\
data_raw/strong_motion_query_status.parquet\
data_processed/catalogue_with_felt_mt_strong.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 5 \'97 Build the attenuation dataset\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Joins every Felt RAPID spatial cell to its associated earthquake using 
\fs26 publicid
\fs24 . It calculates paired epicentral and approximate hypocentral distances and creates modelling eligibility and exclusion flags.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_dataset_all.parquet\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_dataset.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 6 \'97 Approximate rupture distance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Uses recognised moment magnitude and moment-tensor nodal-plane geometry to estimate rectangular rupture dimensions and candidate rupture distances.\
Candidate rupture distances are calculated for both nodal planes because the moment tensor does not independently identify the physical rupture plane.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_processed/rupture_geometry.parquet\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_with_Rrup.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 7 \'97 Vs30 and site conditions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Extracts Vs30 values from the New Zealand combined Vs30 raster at each unique Felt RAPID reporting location. It creates continuous Vs30 model terms and descriptive site-condition classes.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 data_processed/vs30_site_lookup.parquet\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_with_site_conditions.parquet\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_final_dataset.parquet\
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Script 8 \'97 Intensity attenuation modelling\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Fits and compares mixed-effects intensity attenuation models.\
The response variable is reported MMI. Candidate predictors include:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
magnitude;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
source-to-site distance;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
earthquake depth;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Vs30;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
tectonic region;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
fault style;\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
magnitude-distance interaction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Earthquake ID is included as a random intercept to account for multiple Felt RAPID observations from the same event.\
Candidate models are fitted with maximum likelihood for comparison. The selected model is refitted with restricted maximum likelihood for final coefficient estimates.\
Main outputs:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 models/NZ_FR_IAR_final_model.rds\
models/NZ_FR_IAR_selected_model_ML.rds\
models/NZ_FR_IAR_candidate_models_ML.rds\
\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_model_sample.parquet\
data_processed/NZ_FR_IAR_with_model_results.parquet\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

