\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 MODELLING NOTES\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Felt RAPID MMI is an ordered intensity measure, but the principal model treats it as approximately continuous so that predictions and attenuation coefficients can be interpreted directly.\
The mixed-effects approach accounts for the clustering of many reporting cells within the same earthquake through an earthquake-level random intercept.\
The principal model initially uses hypocentral distance because it is available for nearly all eligible observations. Approximate rupture distance should be evaluated as a sensitivity analysis.\
Site condition should normally be represented by the continuous 
\fs26 ln_Vs30_over_760
\fs24  term. The categorical site classes are primarily descriptive.\
Tectonic region and fault style are only included where there are enough observations and earthquakes within multiple usable categories.\
All candidate models are fitted to the same complete-case sample before comparing AIC, BIC, or likelihood-ratio statistics.\
}